<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15847" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ē-nūbo</span></b> , psi, 3,
			v. n. (a Livian word). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To marry out of one's rank</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">e patribus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					4, 4, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">10, 23,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In gen., <i>to marry</i> and leave the paternal house,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				26, 34, 3</span></i>, v. Weissenb. ad <i><span class="en">Liv. 39,
				19, 5</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
